{"data":{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.22551146","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.5281/zenodo.22551146","prefix":"10.5281","suffix":"zenodo.22551146","identifiers":[{"identifier":"oai:zenodo.org:22551146","identifierType":"oai"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"alternateIdentifierType":"oai","alternateIdentifier":"oai:zenodo.org:22551146"}],"creators":[{"name":"Atwell, Casey","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Casey","familyName":"Atwell","nameIdentifiers":[],"affiliation":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"A Short Resolution of Zhao's Open Problem 5.2 after the 2026 Jacobian Counterexample"}],"publisher":"Zenodo","container":{},"publicationYear":2026,"subjects":[{"subject":"Hessian nilpotent polynomials"},{"subject":"formal power series"},{"subject":"Vanishing Conjecture"},{"subject":"Jacobian conjecture"},{"subject":"Zhao Open Problem 5.2"},{"subject":"Laplacian"},{"subject":"disjoint formal power series"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2026-09-06","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":null,"types":{"ris":"GEN","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"article","schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceType":"","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint"},"relatedIdentifiers":[{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"10.1090/S0002-9947-06-03898-0","resourceTypeGeneral":"JournalArticle","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"10.4064/ap93-2-3","resourceTypeGeneral":"JournalArticle","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.21554281","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"Cites","relatedIdentifier":"https://isa-afp.org/entries/Jacobian_Counterexample.html","resourceTypeGeneral":"Software","relatedIdentifierType":"URL"},{"relationType":"IsVersionOf","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.22551145","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"}],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"1.0.0","rightsList":[{"rights":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","rightsUri":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rightsIdentifier":"cc-by-4.0","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"Zhao asked in 2008 whether the Vanishing Conjecture can fail for a nonpolynomial Hessian-nilpotent formal power series over C. The 2026 failure of the Jacobian Conjecture, combined with Zhao's 2007 equivalence, supplies a homogeneous quartic Hessian-nilpotent polynomial P0 for which the Vanishing Conjecture fails. We adjoin two fresh variables and a nonpolynomial isotropic tail R=q(u+iv). Zhao's own disjoint-sum identity then gives exact additivity of Delta^m P^(m+1), while every power of R is harmonic. Hence P0+R is a nonpolynomial Hessian-nilpotent formal power series for which the Vanishing Conjecture fails. This closes Open Problem 5.2. The mechanism is principally a post-2026 corollary of Zhao's published machinery; priority is not claimed.","descriptionType":"Abstract"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22551146","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":0,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"api","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":3,"citationCount":0,"citationsOverTime":[],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":1,"created":"2026-09-06T19:57:56.000Z","registered":"2026-09-06T19:57:56.000Z","published":"2026","updated":"2026-09-06T19:57:56.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"cern.zenodo","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"cern","type":"providers"}},"media":{"data":{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.22551146","type":"media"}},"references":{"data":[{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.21554281","type":"dois"},{"id":"10.4064/ap93-2-3","type":"dois"},{"id":"10.1090/s0002-9947-06-03898-0","type":"dois"}]},"citations":{"data":[]},"parts":{"data":[]},"partOf":{"data":[]},"versions":{"data":[]}